WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.972 --> 00:00:05.972
(keyboard clacking)

00:00:08.142 --> 00:00:10.725
(lively music)

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.663
- All set.

00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:20.210
265 vaccination appointments booked.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.840
- [Joanna] Allow me to clarify.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.020
That's over 200 COVID vaccine appointments

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.570
booked by this guy.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.630
- Hi, I'm Kris Slevens.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.130
I'm an unemployed IT geek from New Jersey

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.740
doing my best to secure
COVID vaccine appointments

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.600
for seniors in my community.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.430
- [Joanna] In case you
haven't had the pleasure

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.620
of booking a COVID vaccine online,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.200
it can suck.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.320
And not only for people who
aren't great at computers.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.170
I just found a COVID vaccine appointment

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.690
for an 80-year-old family
friend on Rite Aid,

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.370
and then a couple of
minutes later it was gone.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.380
I just feel like I don't know
how to work the internet.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.820
The websites all differ.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.300
They're hard to navigate and
appointments are very limited.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.580
- Honestly, I'd equate it to a joint

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.740
sneaker release between
Beyonce and Coldplay

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.240
that included free concert tickets.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.420
It's a shame, but that's where we are

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.130
due to the fragmented rollout.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.350
- [Joanna] Kris fist set out to book

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.700
71 appointments for seniors,

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.140
71 for his father who passed
away at the age of 71,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.490
possibly from COVID itself.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.650
But after Kris had a
booking system in place,

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.410
he just kept going.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.343
So I decided to go study under the master

00:01:27.343 --> 00:01:30.693
and get his best tips
on booking appointments.

00:01:32.177 --> 00:01:33.950
- Nice to meet you, I'm Kris.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.192
- [Both] COVID bump.

00:01:35.192 --> 00:01:38.367
- How intense is it in this
world of vaccine booking?

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:41.684
- Right now we're at a point
where milliseconds matter.

00:01:41.684 --> 00:01:43.860
That's why I always try and suggest

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.670
using a desktop or laptop
over a mobile phone.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.958
- [Joanna] And don't worry

00:01:48.958 --> 00:01:49.791
if you don't live here in New Jersey.

00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:51.800
I was able to use his
tips to book appointments

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.220
in New York, Maryland and Florida.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.640
Plus I had Kris highlight specific tips

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.560
for nationwide pharmacy sites,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.600
such as Rite Aid and CVS.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.630
Okay, on to the tips.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.550
Step one, bookmark the websites
and learn the patterns.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.720
Gather and bookmark the
links to the websites

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.020
that allow you to make
appointments in your area.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.330
- My best suggestion would be

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.260
check your state resources

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.770
or if there are Facebook groups
such as ours in New Jersey,

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:23.250
we post every single
availability in real time.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.201
- [Joanna] In some states there have been

00:02:25.201 --> 00:02:27.910
aggregation sites built that
list all the vaccine locations.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.900
Facebook groups can also be very helpful

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.117
for knowing the patterns when
new appointments are added.

00:02:33.117 --> 00:02:35.620
- [Kris] CVS I would
always suggest checking

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.470
at five AM to six AM.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.260
That's when they load appointments.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.750
For Rite Aid, I would
suggest always checking

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.600
at 11:50 PM at night.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.520
- Do you sleep at all?

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.620
- Most recently not a lot.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.340
Maybe two, three hours a night.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.220
- [Joanna] Rite Aid and
CVS would not confirm

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.720
those appointment drop times,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.210
but I had similar luck
at booking around then.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.130
Step two: set up autofill
in your web browser.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.950
- You're able to fill your address,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.570
name, phone number and
email address ahead of time,

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:07.000
be it in Chrome or any
other web browser you have

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.000
so when it comes time
to click that booking

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.660
you can automatically
filly that information

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.630
without having to type it all in one go.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.180
- [Joanna] All browsers have this.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:21.770
In Chrome, go to preferences,
autofill, addresses and more.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:25.030
And Microsoft Edge, go to
preferences, personal info.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.670
In Safari, preferences, autofill.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:31.470
One thing you cannot autofill,
your insurance information.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.200
But you can skip putting
that info in altogether

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.530
on sites light Rite Aid and CVS.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.440
Step three: set up browser extensions.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.170
Now you're ready to book.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.010
Just the little problem of figuring out

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.240
when the websites have appointments.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.100
Two tools Kris uses are necessary.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:52.300
The first: a browser refresh
extension called Page Refresh.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.010
This allows you to refresh the site

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.880
every few seconds or
minutes without any clicking

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.620
so you can see if it's been updated

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.680
with new appointment times.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.490
Kris keeps these windows
open on his second monitor

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.750
so he can see them at all times.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.980
This extension is available
for Chrome and Microsoft Edge,

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.600
and the developer clearly states

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.330
the extension doesn't
collect any user data.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.370
- Keep the page refreshing,

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.900
but make sure to also
keep the extension open

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.680
so you can stop it in an instant

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.390
and get started on booking.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.500
- [Joanna] If you don't hit stop,

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.010
it could refresh the page

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.020
and you could lose the
appointment opening.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:27.620
The second tool is really cool.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.260
It's called Visual Ping.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.180
You input a website and you tell it

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.740
to watch a certain part
of it, an image or text.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.040
If there's a change to it,

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.180
it will alert you with an email.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:40.400
You can also use the free web extension

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.238
and get alerted with a sound.

00:04:42.238 --> 00:04:43.120
(notification chiming)

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.793
- Every website will say

00:04:44.793 --> 00:04:47.160
there are no appointments available.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.890
If you go in, select that
element in Visual Ping,

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.810
have it alert you when that's gone,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.410
you'll be able to score
an appointment easily.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.970
- [Joanna] I did that on this website here

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:58.200
and was able to book an
appointment that way.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.200
The downside is that you have to upgrade

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.160
to one of the higher
tiers to have the tool

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.560
watch for changes to your
site every five minutes.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.290
The web extension is free,

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.710
but you have to be at a
computer to be notified.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.360
Do you think that when we
publish this by next week,

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.570
you'll hit 300?

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.403
- Easily.

00:05:13.403 --> 00:05:17.210
Until it gets as easy to
schedule a COVID vaccine shot

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.663
as a flu shot, I'm gonna be continuing.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.210
As rough as it is, it's a good feeling

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.460
to be able to get a senior an appointment

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.552
who would not have been able to otherwise.

00:05:29.552 --> 00:05:32.302
(cheerful music)

